+## Purpose
 
-## What alpha3 adds
+Alpha4 hardens the recording layer discovered by the first full 7,169-file alpha3 desktop run. It keeps the Broadcast → Recording → Physical File model, but refuses to call a recording family trustworthy when filename lineage, multipart numbering, duration families, or same-date slot coverage contradict it.
 
-- classifies recording families as complete captures, complete multipart assemblies, likely-complete captures, partials, fragments, truncated files, incomplete multipart sets or unknown-duration recordings;
-- keeps a complete standalone capture separate from a multipart assembly of the same broadcast;
-- compares assembled multipart duration with the longest known capture;
-- ranks one preferred recording candidate while preserving every alternate recording and physical location;
-- propagates complete-hash and strong fingerprint conflicts across different show/date/slot identities;
-- identifies a small suspicious-merge queue where substantial same-date captures may be separate programme occurrences;
